confirming": 5, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [{"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "confirm"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B2", "B1.2"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=100%, source=both]\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloid Neoplasm in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal/excessive bleeding, anemia, bone pain, confusion\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Chronic Myeloid Neoplasm in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal/excessive bleeding, anemia, bone pain, confusion\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\nRelated to De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia: acute disease, acute leukemia of ambiguous lineage, acute myeloid leukemia with mutated npm1\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → pain → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts"}
